      "sourceText": "比较形象一点的说法：当前线程主动告诉操作系统调度器：“我现在可以先让一下 CPU，你可以考虑让别的线程先运行。”\n`yield()` 只是“主动让出这次 CPU 调度机会”，但马上又被调度回来也是完全可能的。",
      "translatedText": "To put it more vividly: the current thread actively tells the operating system scheduler: \"I can yield the CPU for now, and you may consider letting another thread run first\\.\" `yield()`It merely \"voluntarily gives up this CPU scheduling opportunity,\" but it is entirely possible that it will immediately be scheduled back\\.",
